Apache-2.0. DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code. The outside-session lanes
DECZERO, COURIER, YYMIX, XBIRTH and WEBS are DreamingOfClouds'. Parts of the analysis (the Clone lemma,
the b-family, M45 as the B-port contract) were Fable-assisted and reproduced independently by our lanes.

data/base-7546-word.json.gz is the #7546 word by ToikY (bytes of expected/role902-WORD.json.gz at #7546 head
99438c43df7aac1e5dbcc43c1578fcd886c119ec, SHA256 pinned in words.py); credit ToikY. The unpaid words in Part III
are our own edits of it, shipped as edit lists (data/edits-*.json.gz, data/window8-targets.json.gz).

data/W6805.json.gz is CubeJerry's #6805 word, used as data only by cuts.py; credit CubeJerry.
No code from that PR is run. The feeder6805 edit list (data/edits-feeder6805.json.gz) is our own (an outside-session lane, Fable-assisted), and data/mix14-bprime-R.json is our own lane data.

data/lines120.json (Gram and F2^9 labels of the 120 E8 lines, the first 104 being the P104 ports) is our derived
data, checked against the repository file research/complex-frame-pair-decoders/inputs/pr717/P104_HIT_flip_3a.txt
(PR968 decoder, pinned in SOURCES.json) through data/iso968.json, as in #7583; credit the PR968 authors.
